**Reading the pin and driving an output.** A program configures pins as input or output, then repeatedly reads and acts. With an active-low button, the logic must test for LOW:

```
pinMode(BUTTON, INPUT_PULLUP);   // input with pull-up
pinMode(LED, OUTPUT);
loop() {
  if (digitalRead(BUTTON) == LOW)  digitalWrite(LED, HIGH);  // pressed: LED on
  else                              digitalWrite(LED, LOW);
}
```

Note the inversion: pressed is LOW, but we want the LED ON.
